<title>USA: Air Methods to team up with Boeing.</title>
<headline>Air Methods to team up with Boeing.</headline>
<dateline>DENVER 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Air Methods Corp said early Wednesday that it has been selected to team up with the helicopters division of Boeing Co's Defense and Space Group to pursue the Canadian search and rescue helicopter program.</p>
<p>The program includes 15 new search and rescue helicopters to be completed over a period of three to four years, the company said, adding that it believed the Canadian government was to award a contract in the second half of 1997.</p>
<p>The company did not say what the program would be worth.</p>
<p>Air Methods provides emergency air medical transportation systems and services to hospitals throughout the United States.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
